Under Article 19(1) of Regulation (EU) No 1169/2011, the following foods are exempt from displaying a list of ingredients [REG_1169_2011, Article 19]:

(a) Fresh fruit and vegetables, including potatoes, which have not been peeled, cut or similarly treated [REG_1169_2011, Article 19];
(b) Carbonated water, the description of which indicates that it has been carbonated [REG_1169_2011, Article 19];
(c) Fermentation vinegars derived exclusively from a single basic product, provided that no other ingredient has been added [REG_1169_2011, Article 19];
(d) Cheese, butter, fermented milk and cream, to which no ingredient has been added other than lactic products, food enzymes and micro-organism cultures essential to manufacture, or in the case of cheese other than fresh cheese and processed cheese, the salt needed for its manufacture [REG_1169_2011, Article 19];
(e) Foods consisting of a single ingredient, where:
   (i) the name of the food is identical to the ingredient name; or
   (ii) the name of the food enables the nature of the ingredient to be clearly identified [REG_1169_2011, Article 19].
